From: coolsnowwolf <coolsnowwolf@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] qca-nss-dp: preserve 64-bit XGMAC MIB counters

All fal_xgmib_info_t fields are 64-bit. Reading them as uint32_t
truncates the ethtool statistics, including byte and pause counters.
Use a 64-bit load as already done for the data-plane statistics.

Signed-off-by: coolsnowwolf <coolsnowwolf@gmail.com>

--- a/hal/gmac_ops/syn/xgmac/syn_if.c
+++ b/hal/gmac_ops/syn/xgmac/syn_if.c
@@ -271,7 +271,7 @@
 		p = ((uint8_t *)(&mib_stats) +
 			syn_gstrings_xmib_stats[i_mib].stat_offset);
 		i = SYN_STATS_LEN + i_mib;
-		data[i] = *(uint32_t *)p;
+		data[i] = *(uint64_t *)p;
 	}
 
 	return 0;
